<article class="prose">
  <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
  <h1>Registered accounts</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mark a TFSA, RRSP, or RESP on an account. Contribution room is an estimate from what you enter, not tax advice.</p>

  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2>1. Mark the account</h2>
      <p>The section is on a Cash account or a tracking account that holds assets. A credit card does not get it.</p>
      <p>Open the account. Under <strong>Registered account</strong>, turn on <strong>Track as registered</strong>. Choose <strong>TFSA</strong>, <strong>RRSP</strong>, or <strong>RESP</strong>.</p>
      <p>For a TFSA or an RRSP, pick an <strong>Owner</strong>, or add one with <strong>New person…</strong>. A second account for the same person joins that person’s plan. It does not start a second pool of room.</p>
      <p>An RRSP can be a <strong>Spousal RRSP</strong>. The plan stays with the owner. <strong>Spouse</strong> is whose room new deposits use. When the budget has more than one person, pick that spouse before you save.</p>
      <p>For an RESP, add <strong>Beneficiaries</strong>. <strong>New child…</strong> asks for a name and a birth year. Save needs the birth year. Two or more beneficiaries is a family plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="step-shot">
        <img class="shot-light" src="/images/guides/registered-account.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="The account editor, with Track as registered on and RRSP selected.">
        <img class="shot-dark" src="/images/guides/registered-account-dark.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="The account editor, with Track as registered on and RRSP selected.">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2>2. Read the room</h2>
      <p>Open <strong>Reports</strong> and <strong>Registered Room</strong>. Each plan shows a meter: <strong>Room available</strong>, <strong>Approaching limit</strong>, <strong>Maxed out</strong>, <strong>Over-contributed</strong>, or <strong>New room available</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Show my calculation</strong> lists how the app got there. <strong>Confirmed room</strong> is the figure you enter. On an RRSP that section is <strong>CRA room (Notice of Assessment)</strong> and <strong>Available room (CRA)</strong>, with an as-of date. The app does not build RRSP room from your income.</p>
      <p>A TFSA withdrawal can return as room the next year. An RRSP or RESP withdrawal does not.</p>
      <p>If the meter says <strong>Over-contributed</strong>, the penalty line is an estimate. The screen says it is not tax advice.</p>
      <p>When the owner’s birth year says they are 71 or older, the RRSP plan shows a reminder about maturing the plan. That reminder is not tax advice, and the app does not convert the account for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="step-shot">
        <img class="shot-light" src="/images/guides/registered-room.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="Registered Room, with a meter for each plan.">
        <img class="shot-dark" src="/images/guides/registered-room-dark.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="Registered Room, with a meter for each plan.">
      </figure>
      <figure class="step-shot">
        <img class="shot-light" src="/images/guides/registered-rrsp.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="An RRSP plan, with its contribution room meter.">
