  <section class="guide-split">
    <div class="copy">
      <h2>3. Record a deposit</h2>
      <p>A transfer into the plan usually counts as a <strong>Contribution</strong>. On the transaction you can set <strong>Withdrawal</strong>, <strong>Principal transfer</strong>, or <strong>Exempt (no room effect)</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Exempt</strong> is for a market change, a dividend, or a Home Buyers’ Plan or Lifelong Learning Plan repayment. The RRSP plan has a <strong>Room effect tip</strong> that says this. The app does not keep a repayment schedule for those plans.</p>
      <p>A <strong>Principal transfer</strong> is a move between plans of the same type for the same person. It does not use room.</p>
      <p>On a spousal RRSP, the deposit uses the spouse’s room unless you change it on that transaction.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="step-shot">
        <img class="shot-light" src="/images/guides/registered-deposit.jpg" width="800" height="1739" alt="A new transaction, with Registered effect set to Exempt.">
